# runner_registration_exemptions.list -- documented exceptions to the
# invariant scripts/check-runner-registration.py enforces: every test file
# tests/ci_smoke.sh actually invokes must also be invoked by
# tests/run_all.sh (what `make box-check` actually runs), because
# otherwise a box-check "green" proves nothing about a ci_smoke-only gate
# (issue #433). A deliberate, legitimate exception goes here, one per line:
#
#   filename|reason
#
# '#' comments and blank lines are ignored. No entry here means "no known
# legitimate exceptions" -- it does NOT mean the guard has nothing to check;
# run scripts/check-runner-registration.sh and read its output.
#
# As of this file's creation (issue #433), two real, UNDOCUMENTED gaps
# exist and are deliberately NOT listed below: tests/test_capture_smoke.py
# and tests/test_uprobe_fired.py are both invoked only by tests/ci_smoke.sh.
# Both look like genuine reconciliation gaps (not a deliberate CI-only
# design -- see each file's own docstring), so they are left for
# scripts/check-runner-registration.sh to report rather than silenced here;
# fixing them means wiring them into tests/run_all.sh's LIVE_TESTS, which is
# a live-tier test-assertion change out of scope for the guard-building
# commit that added this file.
